>The Cambodian Experience</article-title><source>Trauma, War and violence: Public mental health in sociocultural context</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>New York: Plenum-Kluwer</publisher-name><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>155</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bronfenbrenner</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><source>The ecology of human development: experiments by nature and design</source><year>1979</year><publisher-name>Cambridge, Mass.: Harvard University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hobfoll</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name></person-group><source>Stress, culture, and community: the psychology and philosophy of stress</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>New York: Plenum Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dalton</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Elias</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wandersman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>Community psychology: linking individuals and communities</source><year>2007</year><edition>2</edition><publisher-name>Belmont, Calif.: Thomson Wadsworth</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Somasundaram</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>van de Put</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Eisenbruch</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>de Jong Joop</surname><given-names/></name></person-group><article-title>Starting Mental Health Services in Cambodia</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>1999</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>1029</fpage><lpage>1046</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10390042</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vickery</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><source>Cambodia: 1975&#x02013;1982</source><year>1984</year><publisher-name>Boston, MA: South End Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoole</surname><given-names>MRR</given-names></name><name><surname>Somasundaram</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Thiranagama</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sritharan</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><source>Broken Palmyra</source><year>1990</year><publisher-name>California: Sri Lanka Studies Institute</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.uthr.org/BP/Content.htm"/></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organization</collab></person-group><source>Mental Disorders: Glossary and Guide to their Classification in Accordance with the Ninth Revision of the International Classification of Diseases, Tenth revision (ICD-10)</source><year>1992</year><publisher-name>Geneva: WHO</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jeyanthy</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Loshani</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sivarajini</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A study of Psychological Consequences of Displacement on Family Members</article-title><source>MBBS thesis</source><year>1993</year><publisher-name>University of Jaffna, Dept. Of Community Medicine</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Sphere Project</collab></person-group><source>Sphere Handbook-Humanitarian Charter and Minimum Standards in Disaster Response, Revised Edition</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Oxford, Oxfam Publishing</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.sphereproject.org/handbook"/></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Department of Mental Health and Substance Dependence, World Health Organization</collab></person-group><source>Disaster Mental Health-Mental and Social Aspects of Health of Populations Exposed to Extreme Stressors</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Geneva: WHO</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Inter-Agency Standing Committee</collab></person-group><source>IASC Guidelines on Mental Health and Psychosocial Support in Emergency Settings</source><year>2007</year><publisher-name>Author: Geneva</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tribe</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A Critical Review of the Evolution of a Multi-level Community-based Children's Play Activity Programme Run by the Family Rehabilitation centre (FRC) Throughout Sri Lanka</article-title><source>Journal of Refugee studies</source><year>2004</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>114</fpage><lpage>135</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tribe</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><collab>Family Rehabilitation Centre Staff</collab></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Miller K, Rasco L</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Internally Displaced Sri Lankan War Widows: The Women's Empowerment Programme</article-title><source>The Mental Health of Refugees: Ecological approaches to Healing and Adapt ion</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>New York: Lawrence Earlbaum</publisher-name><fpage>161</fpage><lpage>168</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Armenian</surname><given-names>HK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Perceptions from Epidemiological Research in an Endemic War</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>1989</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>643</fpage><lpage>647</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2711217</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zwi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ugalde</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Towards an Epidemiology of Political Violence in the Third World</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>1989</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>633</fpage><lpage>646</lpage><comment>See also whole special issue of <italic>Soc Sci Med </italic>1989, 28 (7): 631&#x02013;767.</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2652321</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lopez</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Mathers</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Ezzati</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jamison</surname><given-names>DT</given-names></name><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>CJL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Global and regional burden of disease and risk factors, 2001: systematic analysis of population health data</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2006</year><fpage>1747</fpage><lpage>1757</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16731270</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation ci